Third-party attributions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The packages in this repository depend on third-party open-source libraries,
each under its own licence (all on the allowlist in AGENTS.md: Apache-2.0, MIT,
BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, Unicode-DFS-2016, 0BSD,
CC0-1.0, MPL-2.0). The full dependency lists and their licences are produced by
"make license" in each language folder:

  typescript/  npm dependencies        (license-checker-rseidelsohn)
  rust/        crates.io dependencies  (cargo-deny, rust/deny.toml)
  go/          Go modules              (go-licenses)
  python/      PyPI dependencies       (pip-licenses)
  java/        Maven dependencies      (license-maven-plugin)

Code copied or adapted from other projects is listed below with its source,
copyright and licence.

  CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md is adapted from the Contributor Covenant, version 2.1,
  https://www.contributor-covenant.org, licensed under CC BY 4.0.

  The tracing setup uses the official OpenTelemetry SDKs and OTLP exporters
  as dependencies (Copyright The OpenTelemetry Authors, Apache-2.0). The OTLP
  data model and field names (opentelemetry-proto, Apache-2.0) are used for
  interoperability; no .proto files are copied into the packages.

  The Datadog propagator, the 64/128-bit id conversion and the log
  correlation format implement the publicly documented Datadog header and
  tag formats (x-datadog-trace-id, x-datadog-parent-id,
  x-datadog-sampling-priority, x-datadog-tags/_dd.p.tid, dd.trace_id,
  dd.span_id). They were written independently and checked against the
  output of Datadog's ddtrace library (Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause) used only as
  a test oracle; no ddtrace code is copied. The recorded vectors are in
  the test fixtures (propagation.*.vectors.json, toDatadogTraceId.vectors.json,
  traceFields.ddtrace_log_correlation.json).

  The query client uses the request and response field names of the public
  Datadog API v2 (spans events search, spans analytics aggregate, APM
  services, validate_keys, trace by id). Test fixtures named
  *.docs_example.json (typescript/test/fixtures, rust/tests/fixtures/dd,
  go/testdata, python/tests/fixtures, java/src/test/resources/fixtures) are
  copies of examples from Datadog's published OpenAPI specification
  (DataDog/datadog-api-client-python, .generator/schemas/v2/openapi.yaml,
  Copyright Datadog, Inc., Apache-2.0). The other fixtures were recorded from
  datadog/agent 7.85.4 and datadog/fakeintake v79 in the Docker test stack.

  Test-only components (not part of any published package): the Docker
  suite runs the datadog/agent image (Apache-2.0 Agent; the image is
  distributed by Datadog under its own terms) and datadog/fakeintake
  (Apache-2.0). docker/trace-reader/reader.py decodes the Agent's trace
  payloads; it was written from the public .proto definitions in
  DataDog/datadog-agent (pkg/proto/datadog/trace, Apache-2.0) and copies no
  Datadog code.
